WEBVTT

00:00.323 --> 00:00.857
- [Voiceover] All right,

00:00.857 --> 00:03.434
we're told that the
arithmetic sequence a-sub-i

00:03.434 --> 00:07.869
is defined by the formula where
the ith term in the sequence

00:07.869 --> 00:10.330
is going to be 4 plus 3

00:10.330 --> 00:12.698
times i minus 1.

00:12.698 --> 00:14.788
What is a-sub-20?

00:14.788 --> 00:17.226
And so a-sub-20 is the
20th term in the sequence

00:17.226 --> 00:18.642
and I encourage you to pause the video

00:18.642 --> 00:21.568
and figure out what is the 20th term?

00:21.568 --> 00:23.356
Well, we can just think
about it like this.

00:23.356 --> 00:27.930
A-sub-20, we just use this
definition of the ith term.

00:27.930 --> 00:30.368
Everywhere we see an i,
we would put a 20 in,

00:30.368 --> 00:35.368
so it's going to be 4 plus 3 times 20

00:35.755 --> 00:37.148
minus 1,

00:37.148 --> 00:40.933
so once again, just to be clear, a-sub-20,

00:40.933 --> 00:43.742
where instead of a-sub-i,
wherever we saw an i,

00:43.742 --> 00:45.460
we put a 20,

00:45.460 --> 00:47.620
and now we can just compute
what this is going to be

00:47.620 --> 00:48.641
equal to.

00:48.641 --> 00:50.453
This is going to be equal to

00:50.453 --> 00:54.377
4 plus 3 times 20 minus 1

00:54.377 --> 00:56.095
is 19.

00:56.095 --> 00:57.975
3 times 19,

00:57.975 --> 01:01.482
let's see, 3 times 19 is 57, right?

01:01.482 --> 01:03.107
It's 30 plus 27, yep.

01:03.107 --> 01:05.684
This is 57,

01:05.684 --> 01:10.467
and 4 plus 57 is equal to 61,

01:10.467 --> 01:13.718
so the 20th term in
this arithmetic sequence

01:13.718 --> 01:16.597
is going to be 61.

01:16.597 --> 01:18.826
Let's do another one of these.

01:18.826 --> 01:20.777
And here, they've told us
the arithmetic sequence

01:20.777 --> 01:23.168
a-sub-i is defined by the formula

01:23.168 --> 01:24.050
a-sub-1,

01:24.050 --> 01:25.560
they gave us the first term,

01:25.560 --> 01:27.231
and they say, every other term,

01:27.231 --> 01:30.691
so a-sub-i, they're defining
it in terms of the previous

01:30.691 --> 01:34.290
terms, so a-sub-i is going
to be a-sub-i minus 1

01:34.290 --> 01:36.055
minus 2,

01:36.055 --> 01:38.516
so this is actually a
recursive definition of

01:38.516 --> 01:39.886
our arithmetic sequence.

01:39.886 --> 01:41.558
Let's see what we can make of this,

01:41.558 --> 01:43.903
so a-sub-5,

01:43.903 --> 01:46.364
a-sub-5 is going to be equal to,

01:46.364 --> 01:48.941
we'll use this second line right here,

01:48.941 --> 01:51.542
a-sub-5 is going to be equal to

01:51.542 --> 01:54.746
a-sub-4 minus 2.

01:54.746 --> 01:56.998
Well, we don't know what
a-sub-4 is just yet,

01:56.998 --> 01:59.111
so let's try to figure that out.

01:59.111 --> 02:02.640
So we could say that a-sub-4 is equal to,

02:02.640 --> 02:04.614
well if we use the second line again,

02:04.614 --> 02:07.841
it's going to be a-sub-3, minus 2.

02:07.841 --> 02:10.233
We still don't know what a-sub-3 is.

02:10.233 --> 02:12.601
I'll keep switching colors
'cause it looks nice.

02:12.601 --> 02:15.829
A-sub-3 is going to be equal to

02:15.829 --> 02:17.802
a-sub-3 minus 1,

02:17.802 --> 02:20.774
so a-sub-2 minus 2.

02:20.774 --> 02:23.352
We still don't know what a-sub-2 is,

02:23.352 --> 02:25.883
and so, we could write,

02:25.883 --> 02:29.064
a-sub-2 is equal to

02:29.064 --> 02:30.643
a-sub-2 minus 1,

02:30.643 --> 02:33.684
so that's a-sub-1 minus 2.

02:33.684 --> 02:35.983
Now, luckily we know what a-sub-1 is.

02:35.983 --> 02:38.885
A-sub-1 is negative 7.

02:38.885 --> 02:41.207
A-sub-1 is negative 7,

02:41.207 --> 02:44.969
so if this is negative 7,

02:44.969 --> 02:48.103
then a-sub-2 is negative 7 minus 2,

02:48.103 --> 02:50.448
which is equal to negative 9.

02:50.448 --> 02:51.888
Well that starts helping us out

02:51.888 --> 02:54.163
because if a-sub-2 is negative 9,

02:54.163 --> 02:55.649
if this is negative 9,

02:55.649 --> 02:57.646
then a-sub-3 is negative 9

02:57.646 --> 02:58.877
minus 2,

02:58.877 --> 03:01.524
which is equal to negative 11.

03:01.524 --> 03:04.937
Well now that we know that
a-sub-3 is negative 11,

03:04.937 --> 03:06.864
so this is negative 11,

03:06.864 --> 03:09.047
we could figure out a-sub-4 is negative 11

03:09.047 --> 03:10.347
minus 2,

03:10.347 --> 03:13.644
which is equal to negative 13.

03:13.644 --> 03:14.875
And we're almost there.

03:14.875 --> 03:16.082
We know a-sub-4,

03:16.082 --> 03:17.893
the fourth term in this
arithmetic sequence

03:17.893 --> 03:19.518
is negative 13,

03:19.518 --> 03:20.633
so,

03:20.633 --> 03:21.376
we can now,

03:21.376 --> 03:23.257
so if this is negative 13,

03:23.257 --> 03:25.393
a-sub-5 is going to be a-sub-4,

03:25.393 --> 03:27.367
which is negative 13 minus 2,

03:27.367 --> 03:30.594
which is equal to negative 15,

03:30.594 --> 03:32.080
so the fifth term in the sequence

03:32.080 --> 03:35.145
is negative 15.

03:35.145 --> 03:36.579
And we're all done.
